        "brand": "STILL INK",
        "scriptPrefix": "Focus",
        "displayLine1": "CLARITY BEFORE",
        "displayLine2": "THE FIRST",
        "displayLine3": "WORD",
        "body": "The best writing rarely begins with noise. It starts in a deliberate, private silence. These five rituals protect that space.",
        "handle": "@stillink",
        "slideId": "Slide 02"
      }
    },
    {
      "layoutId": "body-noir-yellow",
      "slots": {
        "brand": "STILL INK",
        "scriptPrefix": "Begin",
        "displayLine1": "LONGHAND",
        "displayLine2": "BEFORE",
        "displayLine3": "SCREENLIGHT",
        "body": "Three pages by hand, no editing allowed. This untangles the mind and reveals what actually matters before the cursor starts blinking.",
        "handle": "@stillink",
        "slideId": "Slide 03"
      }
    },
    {
      "layoutId": "body-noir-yellow",
      "slots": {
        "brand": "STILL INK",
        "scriptPrefix": "Try",
        "displayLine1": "THE SAME",
        "displayLine2": "CHAIR AT",
        "displayLine3": "THE SAME HOUR",
        "body": "Consistency trains the brain to drop into flow faster. A fixed location becomes a trigger, and the work shows up on cue.",
        "handle": "@stillink",
        "slideId": "Slide 04"
      }
    },
    {
      "layoutId": "body-noir-yellow",
      "slots": {
        "brand": "STILL INK",
        "scriptPrefix": "Focus",
        "displayLine1": "READ ONE",
        "displayLine2": "PERFECT PAGE",
        "displayLine3": "BEFORE WRITING",
        "body": "Ten minutes of prose you admire resets your ear for rhythm. It raises the standard before your own sentences hit the page.",
        "handle": "@stillink",
        "slideId": "Slide 05"
      }
    },
    {
      "layoutId": "body-noir-yellow",
      "slots": {
        "brand": "STILL INK",
        "scriptPrefix": "Try",
        "displayLine1": "WALK IN",
        "displayLine2": "CIRCLES UNTIL",
        "displayLine3": "THE LINE ARRIVES",
        "body": "Motion dissolves mental blocks without forcing them. Many writers pace or stroll until the right phrase finally unlocks itself.",
        "handle": "@stillink",
        "slideId": "Slide 06"
      }
    },
    {
      "layoutId": "body-noir-yellow",
      "slots": {
        "brand": "STILL INK",
        "scriptPrefix": "Begin",
        "displayLine1": "STOP MID",
        "displayLine2": "SENTENCE AND",
        "displayLine3": "STEP AWAY",
        "body": "Hemingway left the last line unfinished to ensure tomorrow started with momentum. Never empty the tank; always leave a thread to pull.",
        "handle": "@stillink",
        "slideId": "Slide 07"
      }
    }
